{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-x5-bring-weight-geometric-content","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:x5-bring-weight-geometric-content","kind":"remark","title":"Geometric content of the weight-$(-1)$ identification","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-x5-bring-weight-identification","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-u1-phase-tube","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-x5-bring-prym-jacobian"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-x5-bring-weight-identification","text":"x5-bring-weight-geometric-content.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:x5-bring-weight-geometric-content\"></a><p>This identification is categorical, not a morphism of curves. By Riemann–Hurwitz, there is no non-constant curve morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{X}_5 \\to \\mathcal{B}_{\\mathrm{Br}}</code> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g = 2 &#x3C; 4</code>). Furthermore, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B}_{\\mathrm{Br}}</code> has no genus-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> Galois quotient because <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_5</code> has no subgroups of index <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code> with the requisite ramification. The proposition instead asserts a compatibility of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}_5</code>-graded observables under the Lagrange ordering.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/x5-bring-weight-geometric-content.md","heading":"Remark","number":"8.3.5","page":"b/rem-x5-bring-weight-geometric-content","qa":{"counts":{"pass":58,"fail":0,"warn":2,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
